From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Venus Build Fix <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026 21:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rpi_arm64: make autoboot uninterruptible

On CM5 the only U-Boot-supported console is uart10. Carriers may leave
that UART inaccessible or its RX input floating, allowing noise to abort
the normal two-second autoboot countdown and strand the appliance at an
invisible U-Boot prompt.

Venus devices boot unattended, so use bootdelay -2 to start bootcmd
immediately without checking the serial input for an abort character.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Venus specific]

---
 configs/rpi_arm64_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/configs/rpi_arm64_defconfig b/configs/rpi_arm64_defconfig
index 38af502940..f182f4d753 100644
--- a/configs/rpi_arm64_defconfig
+++ b/configs/rpi_arm64_defconfig
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@ CONFIG_PCI=y
 CONFIG_EFI_RUNTIME_UPDATE_CAPSULE=y
 CONFIG_EFI_CAPSULE_FIRMWARE_RAW=y
 CONFIG_BOOTSTD_DEFAULTS=y
+CONFIG_BOOTDELAY=-2
 CONFIG_OF_BOARD_SETUP=y
 # CONFIG_USE_BOOTCOMMAND is not set
 CONFIG_FDT_SIMPLEFB=y
-- 
